The loop at $C$ is a scenic drive that leaves town $C$ and returns to $C$ without reaching any other town.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (A) at (0,0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.6,0);
\coordinate (C) at (3.4,2.4);
\coordinate (D) at (1.3,3.6);
\coordinate (E) at (-0.8,2.0);
\draw (A)--(B);
\draw (B)--(C);
\draw (C)--(D);
\draw (D)--(E);
\draw (E)--(A);
\draw (C) .. controls (5.0,1.4) and (5.0,3.4) .. (C);
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[below right] at (B) {$B$};
\node[left] at (C) {$C$};
\node[above] at (D) {$D$};
\node[left] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the degree of vertex $C$?

Two different direct roads join $M$ and $N$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (M) at (2.2,1.4);
\coordinate (N) at (2.0,3.6);
\coordinate (O) at (4.4,1.0);
\coordinate (T) at (0,0.6);
\coordinate (R) at (4.0,3.4);
\draw (M) .. controls (2.53,2.17) and (2.47,2.91) .. (N);
\draw (M) .. controls (1.73,2.09) and (1.67,2.83) .. (N);
\draw (M)--(O);
\draw (M)--(T);
\draw (N)--(R);
\draw (O)--(R);
\fill (M) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (N) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (O) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (T) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (R) circle (2.5pt);
\node[below] at (M) {$M$};
\node[above] at (N) {$N$};
\node[below right] at (O) {$O$};
\node[below left] at (T) {$T$};
\node[above right] at (R) {$R$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What is the degree of vertex $M$?

