The number on each edge is the train journey time in minutes.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.0]
\coordinate (A) at (0,3.0);
\coordinate (B) at (2.6,3.8);
\coordinate (C) at (4.6,2.0);
\coordinate (D) at (3.4,0);
\coordinate (E) at (0.8,0.2);
\draw (A)--(B) node[midway, above] {$22$};
\draw (B)--(C) node[midway, above right] {$47$};
\draw (C)--(D) node[midway, right] {$35$};
\draw (D)--(E) node[midway, below] {$60$};
\draw (E)--(A) node[midway, left] {$28$};
\draw (B)--(E) node[midway, right] {$41$};
\fill (A) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (B) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (C) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (D) circle (2.5pt);
\fill (E) circle (2.5pt);
\node[left] at (A) {$A$};
\node[above] at (B) {$B$};
\node[right] at (C) {$C$};
\node[below] at (D) {$D$};
\node[left] at (E) {$E$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
How long is the direct train journey between $B$ and $E$?

